Before noon, we got a short break.
Jessy and I stood near the back counter.
She took a cup of coffee.
I took a local tea.
I prefer to make my Mexican coffee at home.
"Maya, how is the first day?"
She asked me.
"Very good, Jessy," I said.
"In the beginning, I made a few mistakes."
"But, I made my second coffee well."
"Yes, learning to use the espresso machine is not easy," she said.
Then we talked about Kochi.
"What is your favorite thing in Kochi?"
Jessy asked.
"I really like the rain and food here," I said.
"I am learning to enjoy life in this city."
"You have truly become a Kochi girl now," Jessy said, smiling.
I laughed, but the words stayed with me.
At twelve o'clock, people started coming to the café again.
We started working again.
